cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hebbian Belief-State World Model (HBWM): Study 1"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Patel
    given-names: Cain
repository-code: "https://github.com/CainPatel/hebbian-belief-state-world-model"
url: "https://github.com/CainPatel/hebbian-belief-state-world-model"
abstract: >-
  Study 1 asks whether the plastic synapse state sigma of a BDH ("the Dragon
  Hatchling") core encodes linearly readable beliefs about a partially observed
  9x9 gridworld. Three parameter-matched sequence models (BDH, LSTM, RWKV) are
  trained to predict observations, their internal states are read out with
  standardized linear probes, and four hypotheses (H1 to H4) are decided under
  rules preregistered before any run. The result is a preregistered negative
  one: H1 failed and its kill criterion fired.
keywords:
  - interpretability
  - world models
  - belief states
  - Hebbian plasticity
  - BDH
  - Dragon Hatchling
  - linear probes
  - preregistration
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-27"
